<p>The United States has begun enforcing a naval blockade on ships entering or leaving Iranian ports, with President Trump saying the move is meant to increase pressure on Tehran after peace talks in Islamabad failed and after the recent war disrupted the Strait of Hormuz. US military notices said the measure applies to vessels bound for Iranian ports, while neutral transit to non-Iranian destinations would not be impeded. Iran condemned the blockade as a violation of its sovereignty and warned that it could endanger the fragile ceasefire and raise risks for ports across the Gulf. The move has revived debate over international law, shipping safety, and global energy markets. There were also a few tentative signs that diplomacy might resume: several reports said Washington and Tehran were considering another meeting, and oil prices eased from earlier spikes on hopes that talks could still reopen a path away from further escalation.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/vzYfFJtkqlAzu9m6B7x1aByo8RSDA-By6sdq-eKf0hm8kdQAQ0LGB-hAIUIRQBA3_ENyA8rumlfYJFQMKAZLrw7g-TZCcG4TEnkOaX5g8YZdNRi8zZNa9VY6K9GNsf8WAhvm-jiaunfmhUJRfcln3bjXj8AQuiHrpFOLwPYNfQ8FAY_YnciIuPROSwkRSZG92b6n6BrZM80ks8p1cla8lT-CNzvLNidw0iigxqxQ5so8ii7VWwIhjCikuGK4damNw42vlp6tZe3ztlotOw' alt='A vessel at the Strait of Hormuz, off the coast of Oman’s Musandam province, on April 12.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Oil market: US crude rose to $104.24 a barrel and Brent to $102.29 after the blockade announcement, though benchmark prices later slipped below $100 on hopes that dialogue could resume.</li><li>Shipping flow: Roughly 40 vessels have passed through since the ceasefire began, down from 100 or more per day before the war, showing how far traffic remains below normal.</li><li>Naval scale: CBS reported that the US was using at least 13 warships to enforce the blockade around Iranian ports.</li><li>Economic pressure: The blockade aims to halt most Iranian oil exports, threatening Tehran’s main source of hard currency.</li></ul><blockquote>The imposition of a maritime blockade constitutes a grave violation of the sovereignty and territorial integrity of the Islamic Republic of Iran - Amir Saeid Iravani</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United States: President Trump said the blockade is meant to force Tehran to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and return to negotiations, and he warned that Iranian boats approaching the blockade could be destroyed. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-war-donald-trump-says-us-military-has-blockaded-iranian-ports-to-pressure-tehran-11353646#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Iran: Iranian officials called the blockade piracy and warned that if it continues, no port in the Gulf would be secure, widening the threat beyond Iran’s own coastline. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1991499/us-blockade-of-hormuz-puts-ceasefire-to-test'>Dawn</a>, <a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/4/14/iran-war-live-trump-claims-tehran-wants-a-deal-amid-us-blockade-of-hormuz'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>United Nations: The UN chief urged all sides to respect freedom of navigation in the Strait of Hormuz, reflecting concern that the standoff could disrupt commercial shipping more broadly. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/un-chief-says-all-parties-must-respect-freedom-of-navigation-in-hormuz'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>European governments: Several European countries refused to join the blockade and instead considered a narrower defensive maritime mission, signaling support for maritime security but reluctance to back a US-led interdiction campaign. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1991499/us-blockade-of-hormuz-puts-ceasefire-to-test'>Dawn</a>, <a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/13/world/middleeast/blockade-hormuz-iran-united-states.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Analysts: Multiple outlets said the blockade is a gamble. It may squeeze Iran economically, but it also risks widening the conflict and testing international legal norms. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ckgw8w7mzxgo'>BBC</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-maritime-restrictions-increase-economic-pressure-on-iran/a-76760110'>US maritime restrictions increase economic pressure on Iran</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-slams-us-blockade-as-grave-violation-of-sovereignty-11353740#publisher=newsstand'>Iran Slams US Blockade As &#x27;Grave Violation Of Sovereignty&#x27;</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ckgw8w7mzxgo'>The US blockade of Iran is a gamble. Will it work?</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/us-begins-iran-port-blockade-oil-prices-ease-hopes-dialogue'>US begins Iran port blockade, oil prices ease on hopes for dialogue</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/13/nx-s1-5783804/a-u-s-military-blockade-of-irans-ports-takes-effect-what-does-that-mean'>A U.S. military blockade of Iran&#x27;s ports takes effect. What does that mean?</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://novaramedia.com/2026/04/13/trump-now-threatens-to-block-hormuz-strait/'>Trump Now Threatens to Block Hormuz Strait</a> - novaramedia.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/14/trump-says-the-us-military-has-begun-its-blockade-of-iranian-ports-to-ramp-up-pressure-on-'>Trump says the US military has begun its blockade of Iranian ports to ramp up pressure on Tehran</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-israel-us-war-west-asia-conflict-live-updates-on-april-14-2026-trump-news-today/article70859995.ece'>Israel-Iran war LIVE: Trump vows U.S. will sink any Iran boats that challenge blockade</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/13/trump-vows-us-will-eliminate-any-iranian-ships-that-approach-blockade_6752381_4.html'>Trump vows US will &#x27;eliminate&#x27; a